{"title":"2022 SSMO Relay Round 4 Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Relay_Round_4_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>On each day, a robot finds a new organism with probability <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/5/a3588bb395f693f5fd014687a9b680837fd2dc6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" />, an already discovered organism with probability <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/2/6a270a7be617f39b92e4821298c4555cffe496c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.2$\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" />, and nothing with probability <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/e/b8e15844d523efe58af54649ee285b2c23a96b20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"22\" height=\"13\" />. If a new organism is found, the robot correctly identifies it as new with probability <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/4/27495cbe2044b503d98fb795bb2e0adc0a197062.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.9$\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" />, and if a discovered organism is found, the robot correctly identifies it as discovered with probability <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/4/274c3ed420a60124420c39b147c9a39b6778d0f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.75$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" />. The expected number of days until the robot reports that it has found a new organism can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f583697295fc6f723862c13228ee55107c33ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"34\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Relay_Round_4_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The probability the robot identifies an object as new on a given day is the sum of the probability it finds a new organism and correctly identifies it and the probability it finds a discovered organism and incorrectly identifies it. This is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/a/d2ab4d012b3db66aa20c67783a0a0adca911c86c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[0.7\\cdot0.9+0.2\\cdot(1-0.75)=0.68.\\]\" width=\"255\" height=\"18\" /> Let the expected number of days be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/0/cd0bdccdf62ddb6312a2ef6e4e1b6aa98a3f5b61.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x=0.68\\cdot1+(1-0.68)\\cdot(x+1)\\implies x = \\frac{1}{0.68}=\\frac{25}{17}\\implies 25+17=\\boxed{42}.\\]\" width=\"541\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>~pinkpig\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017135236\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.007 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.020 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 59/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2083/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:26225:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017135236 and revision id 280197. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}